  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "- PDTable: fixed a double vertical scrollbar wherever a table sits directly under an ancestor with a definite height. BC-81 added overflow-x:auto to contain wide columns but left overflow-y unset, and the CSS overflow spec silently coerces an unset overflow-y to auto whenever overflow-x isn't visible - combined with the table's pre-existing height:100%, that let PDTable self-clip and grow its own inner scrollbar stacked on top of whatever was already scrolling the page around it. The base .pdtable rule now uses height:auto, so the table box always matches its own content height and can never have vertical overflow of its own to scroll; overflow-x containment is unaffected. The opt-in MaxHeight/StickyHeader/StickyPager scrollable-table mode keeps its own height:100% via .pdtable-container, so that behaviour is unchanged (BC-81).",
